        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void Manifest::addJob</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>addJob</name>
        <qualifiedname>Manifest::addJob</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Starts one reading of the manifest on the pool thread. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The manifest path and the toolchain argument are copied from the model on the calling thread. The job parses and validates the manifest. It takes the timeout from the daemon table when the manifest is valid, and the default timeout otherwise. A failed validation sets the message. The job then sets the files child on the message thread. The dependency command of a toolchain row blocks until its process ends, so the job does not run on the message thread. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
